B Experimental Setup
B.6 Hyperparameters, Context Windows, Sequence Lengths, and Optimization
Sweep grids.
- DNA/ RNA CPT : learning rate ∈ { 10 -5 , 3 × 10 -4 } , gradient accumulation ∈ { 64 , 128 } , 1 epoch ( 8 runs total).
- Protein SFT data sweep : data fraction ∈ { 20 , 40 , 60 , 80 , 100 } % at 1 epoch.
- Protein RL data sweep : matched data fractions at 1 epoch with β = 10 -4 warm-start; the β = 10 -3 ablation re-runs the same grid.
- Protein RL epoch sweep : epochs ∈ { 1 , 2 , 4 , 8 } at 20% data.
- DNA/ RNA SFT/RL epoch sweep : epochs ∈ { 1 , 2 , 4 , 8 , 16 , 32 } for SFT (capped at 8 for RL), across Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen3-4B, and their post-CPT variants.

--- CHUNK 62 ---
B Experimental Setup
B.7 Compute Resources and Training Budget
All training and evaluation are run on a GPU cluster using NVIDIA H100 (80 GB) and H200 (141 GB) GPUs. We use one GPU per run; multi-node training was not required for any reported result.
- DNA/RNA CPT : 1 × H100, walltime up to 3 days per run. Eight runs ≈ 24 GPU-days.
- Protein SFT : 1 × H100, walltime up to 3 days per run. Eight runs across the reported data and epoch sweeps.
- Protein RL : 1 × H200, walltime up to 7 days per run with automatic checkpointing and requeueing. The reported warm-start β = 10 -4 sweep comprises 8 runs, corresponding to the protein RL results in Figure 4. Each training run chains two GPU evaluation jobs, one for the ID split and one for the OOD split, with sampling at T = 0 . 7 . We did not include the exploratory β = 10 -3 and no-warm-start protein RL runs in the reported results, so they are excluded from the compute accounting here.
- DNA/RNA SFT/RL : 1 × H100, walltime up to 7 days per run. SFT and RL are submitted as chained pairs per backbone, with RL automatically selecting the best SFT checkpoint by validation accuracy.
The dominant reported compute cost is the protein RL sweep: 8 training runs at up to 7 days each ( ≈ 56 H200-days), plus 16 paired ID/OOD evaluation jobs ( ≈ 20 GPU-days). The DNA/RNA CPT and protein SFT sweeps consume the next-largest shares at ≈ 24 GPU-days each.
